  "entry": "code/index.html",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Pick surface markers from the lab's own antibody inventory and have them automatically assigned to the panels and detectors of a 7-colour FACSCanto II. The assignment avoids conflicts, keeps backbone markers fixed, works around the PI live/dead stain and skips unusable vials. The design is then exported as a printable figure and a per-detector CSV. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
